This confirms 42809e6 introduced the `startsWith("metadata.")` logic (working correctly at that point, since `fieldNameForRoutingKey` was not yet normalized). Then c48a5bd broke it by replacing all periods (including the one in "metadata.") with "%2E" before this check runs, causing `startsWith("metadata.")` to always fail for metadata-prefixed keys — exactly what fea5693 fixes by tracking `routingFieldNameInMetadata` as a separate boolean before doing the replacement.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: c48a5bd47fe4f38846fae5dd9b6393e3574fd5e7

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the file history of `StatusUpdaterBolt.java` with `git log --follow` and examined each commit that touched the `fieldNameForRoutingKey` logic, since the fix commit (fea5693) revolves entirely around how `fieldNameForRoutingKey` is normalized and matched against the `"metadata."` prefix.

**(2) Root cause:** Commit `42809e6` ("Allow fieldNameForRoutingKey to be outside metadata...") introduced the logic:
```java
if (fieldNameForRoutingKey.startsWith("metadata.")) {
    builder.field(fieldNameForRoutingKey.substring(9), partitionKey);
}
...
if (!fieldNameForRoutingKey.startsWith("metadata.")) {
    builder.field(fieldNameForRoutingKey, partitionKey);
}
```
This worked correctly at the time, because `fieldNameForRoutingKey` still contained the literal string `"metadata."` with an unescaped period.

Then commit `c48a5bd` ("Normalise fieldNameForRoutingKey; fixes #393") added, in `prepare()`:
```java
if (StringUtils.isNotBlank(fieldNameForRoutingKey)) {
    fieldNameForRoutingKey = fieldNameForRoutingKey.replaceAll("\\.", "%2E");
}
```
This blindly replaces *every* period in the field name — including the period in the `"metadata."` prefix — turning `"metadata.author"` into `"metadata%2Eauthor"`. As a result, the later `startsWith("metadata.")` checks (added by 42809e6) always evaluate to `false` for what should be metadata-routed fields, silently breaking the "store routing key in metadata" feature (the value ends up written outside metadata instead, or field access is corrupted).

**(3) Fix confirmation:** fea5693 fixes exactly this interaction: it adds a `routingFieldNameInMetadata` boolean captured *before* the `%2E` replacement (checking/stripping the `"metadata."` prefix first, then doing the period-escaping), and replaces both `startsWith("metadata.")` checks with this boolean. This is a direct, targeted repair of the bug introduced by the normalization logic in c48a5bd interacting with the metadata-prefix check from 42809e6. Since the check itself was correct until the normalization was added, c48a5bd is the commit that introduced the regression.

I'm confident in this attribution — the diff and logic clearly show the interaction between the two prior commits, and c48a5bd is the one that changed correct behavior into buggy behavior.

